       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. UNDP and Ministry of Environment and Forestry through Montreal Protocol provided Refrigeration and Air Conditioning (RAC) trainers and technicians with good servicing practice training focusing on RAC installation, service and troubleshooting. In 2022, 633 RAC technicians and 54 RAC trainers across Indonesia gained benefits from a series of training to cope up safety aspects while handling HCFCs and newly introduced refrigerants which have higher pressure and flammability compared to HCFCs. These HCFCs contain ozone depleting potential (ODP) and global warming potential (GWP). The training is meant to assure health and safety when the technicians are working in designated locations (houses, buildings, etc).
2. Through the HPMP Stage II project, UNDP facilitated technical support to the Ministry of Environment and Forestry to develop policy and relevant technical guidance to phase-out of HCFC-141b consumption that have been included and enacted under Ministerial Decree of Trade Import Regulation number 18 Year 2021 on goods prohibited for export and goods prohibited for import. The policy and technical guidance are important to protect Indonesia from the importation of products banned by the protocol and assure the health and safety of Indonesian from the danger of HCFCs. UNDP facilitated Indonesia to comply with the schedule of the Montreal Protocol.
3. UNDP facilitated the procurement and distribution of RAC machines and equipment to designated vocational training centres across Indonesia in close coordination with the Ministry of Environment and Forestry and Ministry of Manpower. Through the distribution of these machines and equipment, the training centres are expected to adhere to updated RAC technology being introduced and adopted by the global community.
IS:
1. UNDP has facilitated the Government of Indonesia in the ratification process of the Kigali Amendment to the Montreal Protocol in 2022. The Presidential Regulation Number 129 of 2022 on the Ratification of the Amendment to the Montreal Protocol on Substances that Deplete the Ozone Layer, Kigali, 2016 has been signed by the President on 1 November 2022. Then, on 14 December 2022, the ratification instrument was accepted by the UN depositary. As the amendment is ratified, the Government of Indonesia will start the implementation of the HFC Phase-down in Indonesia starting on 14 March 2023, 90 days after the entry into force.
2. UNDP has been working closely with the Ministry of Environment and Forestry to develop and establish regulatory frameworks able to control the importation and distribution of refrigerants consumed by Refrigeration and Air Conditioning (RAC) installers, manufacturers, and servicing workshops. The project facilitated the release of Ministry of Trade Regulation Number 25/ Year 2022 on the Importation Policy and Regulation of Ozone Depleting Substances (ODS). 
3. UNDP facilitated the Indonesia government to collect, review and report ODS data to Global Ozone Secretariat at timely and effective manner (annually) in compliance with the Montreal Protocol. UNDP facilitated the Government of Indonesia to actively join international meetings, South-South Cooperation and technical discussions. Besides UNDP facilitated International Day of Ozone Layer Protection on 16 September 2022.
4. For the import control of HCFC to Indonesia, HPMP stage II project support capacity building of custom officer through training of ODS import control and indentification of refrigerant. In 2022, trainig for custom has been conducted in 4 location mainly in the border area to prevent the illegal import of control substances</narrative>
